"hadiths[6]{hadithnumber,text}:"
1123,"A man came to Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) and asked about Al-Luqata (a fallen thing). The Prophet (ﷺ) said, Recognize its container and its tying material and then make a public announcement about it for one year and if its owner shows up"
1124,"Narrated Suwaid bin Ghafala:\n\nWhile I as in the company of Salman bin Rabi`a and Suhan, in one of the holy battles, I found a whip. \nOne of them told me to drop it but I refused to do so and said that I would give it to its owner if I \nfound him, otherwise I would utilize it. On our return we performed Hajj and on passing by Medina, I \nasked Ubai bin Ka`b about it. He said, \I found a bag containing a hundred Dinars in the lifetime of \nthe Prophet (ﷺ) and took it to the Prophet (ﷺ) who said to me"
1125,"""I remember it as the Prophet said it."" 'Umar said, ""You are courageous. How did he say it?"" Hudhaifa said, ""A man's affliction (wrong deeds) concerning his wife, money, children, and neighbors are erased by (his) good deeds (righteousness, prayers, charity, fasting, etc.)."" 'Umar said, ""I do not ask about this, but which affliction will spread like the waves of the sea?"" Hudhaifa said, ""The one whose heart is sealed after being exposed to it, will follow it (i.e., succumb to it), and the one whose heart is enlightened (i.e., firm in belief) will not be harmed by it, till it (the seal) is removed like the removal of rust."""
1126,"Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, should serve his guest generously. The guest's reward is: To provide him with a superior type of food for a night and a day and a guest is to be entertained with food for three days, and whatever is offered beyond that, is regarded as something given in charity. And it is not lawful for a guest to stay with his host for such a long period so as to put him in a critical position. Narrated Malik: Similarly as above (156) adding"
1127,"I proceeded till I entered upon `Umar (and while I was sitting there), his gate-keeper Yarfa came to him and said,  `Uthman"
1128,"Narrated `Uqba bin 'Amir:\n\nWe said to the Prophet, \You send us out and it happens that we have to stay with people who do not entertain us. What do you think about it? He said to us"
